(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7215"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7215"), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7215), (:actor/name "Rigging and Cable Splicing Crew Site Coordination Practice"), (:actor/isco-08 "7215"), (:actor/domain :construction/rigging-crew-site-coordination), (:actor/robotics? true), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 10000}"), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :site-verified :worker-verified :effect-propose :closed-op-allowlist :site-mismatch :scope-exclusion)), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "certify the load as lift-ready" "certify the rigging as lift-ready" "finalize the load-rigging certification decision" "finalize the lift-readiness certification decision" "proceed with the lift now" "proceed with the rigging lift" "execute the lift directly" "execute the rigging lift directly" "perform the lift directly" "dispatch the crew to perform the lift" "override the site-safety officer's judgment" "override the site-safety officer" "override the safety officer's lift-readiness judgment" "bypass the load-rigging certification" "bypass the site-safety officer" "bypass lift-readiness sign-off")), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:test/counts "{:total 22, :assertions 52, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :site-verification :worker-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:test/simulator :riggercoord.actor-test), (:adr/id 2799007215), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7215 — Riggers and Cable Splicers Job-Site Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:adr/related (vector "2799007121-cloud-itonami-isco-7121-roofers-coverage" "2799007131-cloud-itonami-isco-7131-painters-and-related-workers-coverage" "2799007214-cloud-itonami-isco-7214-structural-metal-preparers-erectors-coverage")), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7215)), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007215: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7215 Riggers and Cable Splicers job-site scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7215\n-- Riggers and Cable Splicers** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of the\nrollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3 batches 1-2 of ~17 already\nlanded: 7111/7112/7113/7114/7119/7121/7122/7123/7124/7125/7127/7131,\nplus 7214 landed immediately prior to this entry).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7215\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/\nget-occupation \\\"7215\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Riggers and Cable Splicers\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7215` (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7215` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nRiggers prepare loads for crane/hoist lifting and cable splicers\nsplice/inspect wire rope on active job sites -- real physical-safety\nstakes (dropped-load risk, cable-failure risk). The controlling\nconstraint for this vertical is that the closed op allowlist must\nNEVER include any op that directly finalizes a load-rigging/\nlift-readiness certification decision, or overrides a site safety\nofficer's judgment -- those decisions must always be a hard permanent\nblock, never auto-commit-eligible and never merely a soft escalate.\nThis actor is deliberately scoped to JOB-SITE SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS\nCOORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs rigging or cable-splicing work\nitself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored closely for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7121`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7121)\n(Roofers: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph, full doc set, same wave and a similar height/load safety\nshape) -- cloned and read in full in this session, then independently\nre-verified working (22 tests / 52 assertions green) before this\nrepository's own implementation began.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7215` as an OSS job-site\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for riggers and cable\nsplicers, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every\nprior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Rigging\nCoordination Advisor ⊣ RiggerCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned\nidentically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different library\ncoordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **job-site scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct load-rigging/lift-readiness\ncertification authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise,\nsimulate exercising, or propose exercising a load-rigging/\nlift-readiness certification decision, or any override of a\nsite-safety officer's judgment. These are structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely, and are additionally caught as a second,\nindependent free-text scope-exclusion check.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- task/inspection/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task/lift-schedule scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a cable-condition/load-hazard/\n  equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit\n  eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- rigging-equipment procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nload-rigging/lift-readiness certification decision or a\nsite-safety-officer-judgment override. An op such as\n`:finalize-lift-readiness-certification` cannot even be proposed by\nthe reference mock advisor (its `infer` function only ever emits one\nof the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a forged proposal, a\nfuture LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever produced such an op, the\ngovernor's closed-allowlist HARD check (`:unknown-op`) rejects it\nunconditionally and permanently\n(`riggercoord.governor-test/hard-on-unknown-op`). A second,\nindependent HARD check evaluates free-text `:rationale`/`:description`\nfields against `riggercoord.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases` --\nsixteen finalization/execution action phrases (e.g. \"certify the load\nas lift-ready\", \"finalize the lift-readiness certification decision\",\n\"override the site-safety officer's judgment\") -- as defense-in-depth,\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`riggercoord.governor-test/hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-certify-load-lift-ready`,\n`.../hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-override-safety-officer`).\n\n### Six HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Site unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered job site (`:no-site`). Directly implements\n   the CRITICAL invariant that a worker/site record must be\n   independently verified/registered before any action.\n2. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n3. **Op not in closed allowlist** -- any `:op` outside the closed\n   four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`).\n4. **Site mismatch** -- if the proposal names a site, it must be the\n   SAME site verified for this request (`:site-mismatch`) --\n   defense-in-depth against a proposal quietly targeting a different,\n   unverified site.\n5. **Worker unregistered / wrong site** -- if the proposal references\n   a worker, that worker must be a REGISTERED crew member belonging to\n   THIS site (`:unknown-worker` / `:worker-wrong-site`).\n6. **Scope-exclusion violation** -- a proposal whose free-text\n   `:rationale` or `:description` contains a finalization/execution\n   action phrase attempting to finalize a load-rigging/lift-readiness\n   certification decision, or to override a site-safety officer's\n   judgment, is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:scope-exclusion-violation`)\n   -- never overridable by human approval, regardless of confidence or\n   stake.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's `always-escalate-ops` set). This is the ONLY\n  channel by which the robot may surface a cable-condition/\n  load-hazard/equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard\n  data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about site safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-order-cost-threshold` (10000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-or-below-cost-threshold`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  rigging-equipment order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  load-rigging-certification or safety-officer-override attempt, which\n  is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate vs.\n  hard permanent block).\n- advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` (0.6) also escalates, for\n  any op (`escalates-low-confidence`).\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"load\", \"cable\", \"rigging\", \"certification\") can accidentally match\ninside the mock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate\nproposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly\nthe risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a job-site coordination actor\nworking adjacent to load-rigging and cable-splicing necessarily\ndiscusses those concepts to do its scheduling/logging job) could\ntrigger if phrased carelessly.\n`riggercoord.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases` is phrased exclusively\nas finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"certify the load as\nlift-ready\", \"override the site-safety officer's judgment\"), never\nbare nouns, and\n`riggercoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor with rigging/cable\ndomain vocabulary in its request fields (wire rope slings, hoist\ncable, load hook, crane lift), never trips\n`scope-exclusion-violation?`. A companion test\n(`scope-exclusion-not-triggered-by-bare-domain-nouns`) directly asserts\nthat bare nouns like \"load\"/\"cable\"/\"rigging\"/\"certification\" do not\ntrip the guard. Green on first run in this session -- the\nscope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never tripped during\ndevelopment.\n`riggercoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-proposal-with-no-interrupt-path`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nand is never routed through the `:request-approval` interrupt\n(hard `:hold` is a finish point, not an interrupt).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7215\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7215` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7215`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 22 tests, 52 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-lift-readiness-certification`\n  that is merely gated behind an always-escalate list: rejected\n  outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance -- an\n  always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  load-rigging/lift-readiness certification decision exists in the\n  code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision\n  this severe (dropped-load risk, cable-failure risk), the capability\n  itself must not exist. The only op related to site-safety escalation\n  is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for human/site-\n  safety-officer attention and never itself decides, certifies, or\n  defers a load-rigging decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block: rejected per the task's\n  explicit domain design -- an over-threshold rigging-equipment order\n  is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft escalate gate, not\n  a hard block; only the load-rigging-certification/\n  safety-officer-override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"load\" \"cable\"\n  \"rigging\" \"certification\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known\n  self-trip bug class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked\n  example for this exact task), and per the explicit instruction to\n  phrase scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS,\n  never bare nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses\n  load/cable/rigging/certification concepts to do its\n  scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking\n  the actor's own legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly\n  against rationale text that deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Adding a separate `:actor/scope-excluded-ops` list of concretely-named\n  forbidden op keywords (the shape `cloud-itonami-isco-7131` uses, e.g.\n  `:finalize-painting-decision`) as a second independent check layered\n  on top of the closed allowlist: not adopted for this entry -- this\n  repository mirrors the `cloud-itonami-isco-7121` reference exactly,\n  which relies on the closed four-op allowlist (`:unknown-op`) plus the\n  free-text `scope-exclusion-violation?` check as its two independent\n  layers, and both layers are exercised by dedicated tests. A future\n  pass could add named forbidden-op fixtures as further\n  defense-in-depth, consistent with sibling `7131`, without changing\n  the allowlist itself.\n- Merging worker and site into a single entity (only checking one\n  provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered worker AND independently-registered site)\n  matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/site record must be\n  independently verified/registered before any action\" and the\n  established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with\n  two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- task/inspection/progress data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered site, and if a worker is\n   named, an independently registered worker belonging to that site\n   (`:no-site`/`:unknown-worker`/`:worker-wrong-site`). Not a\n   load-rigging or safety-officer decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task/lift-schedule scheduling\n   proposal only. Cannot carry a load-rigging/lift-readiness\n   certification decision (structurally absent from the op's field\n   shape; any such attempt via free text is caught by the\n   `scope-exclusion-violation?` content check). Does not certify,\n   finalize, or draw any conclusion about a specific lift -- it is a\n   calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a cable-condition/\n   load-hazard/equipment-condition concern to a human/site safety\n   officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence\n   level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through\n   which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the site safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- rigging-equipment procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not a load-rigging/lift-readiness\n   certification or authorization decision of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 10000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na load-rigging/lift-readiness certification decision or a\nsite-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`riggercoord.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) the\nindependent HARD `:unknown-op` check\n(`riggercoord.governor-test/hard-on-unknown-op`), and (c) a\ncontent-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op` field\n(`riggercoord.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases`,\n`.../scope-exclusion-violation?`), tested directly against rationale\ntext that attempts to certify a load as lift-ready or override a\nsite-safety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`riggercoord.governor-test/hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-certify-load-lift-ready`,\n`.../hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-override-safety-officer`).\n"), (:db/id -1)))
